IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eca-nouns`
IMPORT `eca-schedules`

-- Employment Claims Act 2016 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition: PART 1, PRELIMINARY (ss 1 and 2).
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively.  Target compiler: main (build 109).
--
-- s 1 (short title) is machinery (inert, reason 2) and has no rule here.
-- s 2(1) is a list of defined terms.  Each is encoded as a function that answers, on facts a witness could state,
-- whether something is that term as the Act defines it, with the members the definition names.
--   * A definition that says "means" is closed: a thing outside it is JUST FALSE (the text's own no).
--   * A definition that says "includes" is open: a thing outside the list answers NOTHING.
--   * A definition that points to another Act ("has the meaning given by ...") is asked as a fact the person states, MAYBE BOOLEAN; "not known" is NOTHING (points outside the text).
--   * A category "prescribed" by regulations is asked as a fact, MAYBE BOOLEAN, for the same reason.

§ `Part 1 -- Preliminary`

§§ `s 2(1) -- definitions`

-- "approved mediator": the five kinds of approval are in eca-nouns.
-- src:123 | 2.—(1) In this Act, unless the context otherwise requires —
-- src:125 | “approved mediator” means any individual approved by the
-- src:126 | Commissioner as a mediator for one or more of the
-- src:127 | following:
-- src:129 | (a) a mediation under Part 2 of a specified employment
-- src:130 | dispute;
-- src:132 | (b) a tripartite mediation;
-- src:134 | (c) a mediation mentioned in section 115(2A) of the
-- src:135 | Employment Act 1968;
-- src:137 | (d) a consultation or conciliation under section 8A(5) of
-- src:138 | the Retirement and Re‑employment Act 1993;
-- src:140 | (e) a mediation or conciliation of any dispute under any
-- src:141 | other written law that the Commissioner may
-- src:142 | determine, being a written law relating to
-- src:143 | employment, employment terms or the relations
-- src:144 | between employers and employees;
@ref s 2(1) “approved mediator” (src:123-144)
GIVEN `the person is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commissioner approved the person as a mediator for` IS A LIST OF `Approval for mediation`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) the person is an approved mediator` MEANS
    IF `the person is an individual` AND NOT (null `the Commissioner approved the person as a mediator for`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“approved mediator” means any individual approved by the Commissioner as a mediator for one or more of the following"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:146 | “authorised person” means an individual appointed under
-- src:147 | section 3(3) of the Employment Act 1968 as an authorised
-- src:148 | person for the purpose of carrying out any function or duty of
-- src:149 | the Commissioner under this Act;
@ref s 2(1) “authorised person” (src:146-149)
GIVEN `the person is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person was appointed under section 3(3) of the Employment Act 1968 as an authorised person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appointment is for carrying out a function or duty of the Commissioner under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) the person is an authorised person` MEANS
    IF `the person is an individual` AND `the person was appointed under section 3(3) of the Employment Act 1968 as an authorised person` AND `the appointment is for carrying out a function or duty of the Commissioner under this Act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“authorised person” means an individual appointed under section 3(3) of the Employment Act 1968 as an authorised person for the purpose of carrying out any function or duty of the Commissioner under this Act"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- "claim": a claim lodged with a tribunal; a counterclaim lodged with a tribunal is one too ("and includes").
-- src:151 | “claim” means a claim lodged with a tribunal, and includes a
-- src:152 | counterclaim lodged with a tribunal;
@ref s 2(1) “claim” (src:151-152)
GIVEN `it is lodged with a tribunal` IS A BOOLEAN
      kind IS A `Kind of claim`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) the thing is a claim` MEANS
    IF `it is lodged with a tribunal`
    THEN CONSIDER kind
         WHEN `A claim` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `A counterclaim` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“claim” means a claim lodged with a tribunal"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:154 | “claim referral certificate” means a claim referral certificate
-- src:155 | issued under —
-- src:157 | (a) section 6(2) or 7(7)(a); or
-- src:159 | (b) section 30H(6) of the Industrial Relations Act 1960;
@ref s 2(1) “claim referral certificate” (src:154-159)
GIVEN `the certificate was issued under` IS A `Provision a certificate was issued under`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) the certificate is a claim referral certificate` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the certificate was issued under`
    WHEN `Section 6(2) of the Employment Claims Act 2016` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `Section 7(7)(a) of the Employment Claims Act 2016` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `Section 30H(6) of the Industrial Relations Act 1960` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“claim referral certificate” means a claim referral certificate issued under"
    WHEN `Some other provision` THEN JUST FALSE

-- "claimant": a person who lodges a claim with a tribunal, and for Part 2 a person who intends to.
-- src:164 | “claimant” means a person who lodges a claim with a tribunal,
-- src:165 | and includes, for the purposes of Part 2, a person who intends
-- src:166 | to lodge a claim with a tribunal;
@ref s 2(1) “claimant” (src:164-166)
GIVEN `the person lodges a claim with a tribunal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person intends to lodge a claim with a tribunal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the question is asked for the purposes of Part 2` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) the person is a claimant` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person lodges a claim with a tribunal` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the question is asked for the purposes of Part 2` AND `the person intends to lodge a claim with a tribunal` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“claimant” means a person who lodges a claim with a tribunal"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:168 | “Commissioner” means the Commissioner for Labour appointed
-- src:169 | under section 3(1) of the Employment Act 1968;
@ref s 2(1) “Commissioner” (src:168-169)
GIVEN `the person was appointed Commissioner for Labour under section 3(1) of the Employment Act 1968` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) the person is the Commissioner` MEANS
    IF `the person was appointed Commissioner for Labour under section 3(1) of the Employment Act 1968`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“Commissioner” means the Commissioner for Labour appointed under section 3(1) of the Employment Act 1968"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- "contract of service": an agreement, oral or written, express or implied (so the form never changes the answer), and an apprenticeship agreement.
-- src:171 | “contract of service” means an agreement, whether oral or
-- src:172 | written and whether express or implied, by which a person
-- src:173 | agrees to employ an individual, and that individual agrees to
-- src:174 | serve that person, and includes an apprenticeship agreement;
@ref s 2(1) “contract of service” (src:171-174)
GIVEN `it is an agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `by it a person agrees to employ an individual` IS A BOOLEAN
      `by it that individual agrees to serve that person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is an apprenticeship agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) the agreement is a contract of service` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `it is an agreement` AND `by it a person agrees to employ an individual` AND `by it that individual agrees to serve that person` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `it is an apprenticeship agreement` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“contract of service” means an agreement, whether oral or written and whether express or implied, by which a person agrees to employ an individual, and that individual agrees to serve that person"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- "court": "competent jurisdiction" is open-textured, so it is a plain input.
-- src:176 | “court” means any court of competent jurisdiction in Singapore;
@ref s 2(1) “court” (src:176)
GIVEN `it is a court in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is of competent jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) the body is a court` MEANS
    IF `it is a court in Singapore` AND `it is of competent jurisdiction`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“court” means any court of competent jurisdiction in Singapore"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- "employee".
-- src:178 | “employee” means an individual who has entered into and
-- src:179 | works under a contract of service with an employer, and
-- src:180 | includes —
-- src:182 | (a) any employee of the Government within a category,
-- src:183 | class or description of such employees prescribed to
-- src:184 | be employees for the purposes of this Act; and
-- src:186 | (b) for an employment dispute relating to the termination
-- src:187 | of a contract of service or any mediation request
-- src:188 | submitted or claim made after the end of a contract of
-- src:189 | service, the former employee who worked under that
-- src:190 | contract of service, even though the relationship
-- src:191 | between employee and employer has ended;
@ref s 2(1) “employee” (src:178-191)
GIVEN `the person is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has entered into a contract of service with an employer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person works under that contract of service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an employee of the Government` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Government employee is in a category, class or description prescribed to be employees for the purposes of this Act` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the dispute is about the termination of a contract of service, or the mediation request or claim is made after the end of a contract of service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person worked under that contract of service` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) the person is an employee` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person is an individual` AND `the person has entered into a contract of service with an employer` AND `the person works under that contract of service` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the person is an employee of the Government` AND `the Government employee is in a category, class or description prescribed to be employees for the purposes of this Act` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the dispute is about the termination of a contract of service, or the mediation request or claim is made after the end of a contract of service` AND `the person worked under that contract of service` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): which categories of Government employees are "prescribed to be employees for the purposes of this Act" is in regulations that are not among the sources
        IF `the person is an employee of the Government` AND `the Government employee is in a category, class or description prescribed to be employees for the purposes of this Act` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“employee” means an individual who has entered into and works under a contract of service with an employer"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- "employer".
-- src:193 | “employer” means any person who employs an individual under
-- src:194 | a contract of service, and includes —
-- src:196 | (a) the Government in respect of any category, class or
-- src:197 | description of employees of the Government
-- src:198 | prescribed to be employees for the purposes of this
-- src:199 | Act;
-- src:201 | (b) a statutory body;
-- src:203 | (c) a person duly authorised by an employer to be the
-- src:204 | employer’s agent or manager;
-- src:206 | (d) a person who owns, carries on or is responsible for
-- src:207 | the management of the profession, business, trade or
-- src:208 | work in which that individual is or was engaged; and
-- src:213 | (e) for an employment dispute relating to the termination
-- src:214 | of a contract of service or any mediation request
-- src:215 | submitted or claim made after the end of a contract of
-- src:216 | service, the former employer, even though the
-- src:217 | relationship between employee and employer has
-- src:218 | ended;
@ref s 2(1) “employer” (src:193-218)
GIVEN `the person employs an individual under a contract of service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the Government` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Government is the employer of a category, class or description of employees prescribed to be employees for the purposes of this Act` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person is a statutory body` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is duly authorised by an employer to be the employer's agent or manager` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person owns, carries on or is responsible for the management of the profession, business, trade or work in which the individual is or was engaged` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the dispute is about the termination of a contract of service, or the mediation request or claim is made after the end of a contract of service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the former employer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) the person is an employer` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person employs an individual under a contract of service` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the person is the Government` AND `the Government is the employer of a category, class or description of employees prescribed to be employees for the purposes of this Act` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the person is a statutory body` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the person is duly authorised by an employer to be the employer's agent or manager` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the person owns, carries on or is responsible for the management of the profession, business, trade or work in which the individual is or was engaged` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the dispute is about the termination of a contract of service, or the mediation request or claim is made after the end of a contract of service` AND `the person is the former employer` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): which categories of Government employees are "prescribed to be employees for the purposes of this Act" is in regulations that are not among the sources
        IF `the person is the Government` AND `the Government is the employer of a category, class or description of employees prescribed to be employees for the purposes of this Act` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“employer” means any person who employs an individual under a contract of service"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- "employment assistance payment": the meaning is given by section 2(1) of the Retirement and Re-employment Act 1993, which is not among the sources.
-- src:220 | “employment assistance payment” has the meaning given by
-- src:221 | section 2(1) of the Retirement and Re‑employment Act 1993;
@ref s 2(1) “employment assistance payment” (src:220-221)
GIVEN `it is an employment assistance payment as section 2(1) of the Retirement and Re-employment Act 1993 gives that meaning` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) the payment is an employment assistance payment` MEANS
    CONSIDER `it is an employment assistance payment as section 2(1) of the Retirement and Re-employment Act 1993 gives that meaning`
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the meaning is "given by section 2(1) of the Retirement and Re-employment Act 1993", which is not among the sources
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST fact THEN
        IF fact
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“employment assistance payment” has the meaning given by section 2(1) of the Retirement and Re-employment Act 1993"
        ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:223 | “Industrial Arbitration Court” means an Industrial Arbitration
