-- "mediation" INCLUDES three things; the list is open, so a thing outside it answers NOTHING.
-- src:227 | “mediation” includes —
-- src:229 | (a) the undertaking of any activity for the purpose of
-- src:230 | promoting the discussion and settlement of disputes;
-- src:232 | (b) the bringing together of the parties to any dispute for
-- src:233 | that purpose, either at the request of one of the parties
-- src:234 | to the dispute or on an order of a tribunal under this
-- src:235 | Act; and
-- src:237 | (c) the follow‑up of any matter which is the subject of
-- src:238 | any such discussion or settlement;
@ref s 2(1) “mediation” (src:227-238)
GIVEN `it is the undertaking of an activity for the purpose of promoting the discussion and settlement of disputes` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is the bringing together of the parties to a dispute for that purpose, at the request of one of the parties or on an order of a tribunal under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is the follow-up of a matter which is the subject of such a discussion or settlement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) the thing is mediation` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `it is the undertaking of an activity for the purpose of promoting the discussion and settlement of disputes` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `it is the bringing together of the parties to a dispute for that purpose, at the request of one of the parties or on an order of a tribunal under this Act` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `it is the follow-up of a matter which is the subject of such a discussion or settlement` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“mediation” includes" three things and does not say that nothing else is mediation
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:240 | “mediation request” means a request for a mediation under
-- src:241 | Part 2;
@ref s 2(1) “mediation request” (src:240-241)
GIVEN `it is a request for a mediation under Part 2` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) the request is a mediation request` MEANS
    IF `it is a request for a mediation under Part 2`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“mediation request” means a request for a mediation under Part 2"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:243 | “mediation session” means a meeting between 2 or more parties
-- src:244 | to a dispute for the purposes of a mediation;
@ref s 2(1) “mediation session” (src:243-244)
GIVEN `the number of parties to a dispute at the meeting` IS A NUMBER
      `it is for the purposes of a mediation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) the meeting is a mediation session` MEANS
    IF `the number of parties to a dispute at the meeting` AT LEAST 2 AND `it is for the purposes of a mediation`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“mediation session” means a meeting between 2 or more parties to a dispute for the purposes of a mediation"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:246 | “Registrar” means the registrar, a deputy registrar or an assistant
-- src:247 | registrar for the tribunals;
@ref s 2(1) “Registrar” (src:246-247)
GIVEN office IS AN `Office for the tribunals`
      `it is an office for the tribunals` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) the officer is a Registrar` MEANS
    IF `it is an office for the tribunals`
    THEN CONSIDER office
         WHEN `The registrar` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `A deputy registrar` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `An assistant registrar` THEN JUST TRUE
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“Registrar” means the registrar, a deputy registrar or an assistant registrar for the tribunals"
         WHEN `Another officer` THEN JUST FALSE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“Registrar” means the registrar, a deputy registrar or an assistant registrar for the tribunals"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:249 | “Registry” means the registry established under section 10(1)
-- src:250 | for the tribunals;
@ref s 2(1) “Registry” (src:249-250)
GIVEN `it is the registry established under section 10(1) for the tribunals` IS A BOOLEAN
