`s 2(1) the registry is the Registry` MEANS
    IF `it is the registry established under section 10(1) for the tribunals`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“Registry” means the registry established under section 10(1) for the tribunals"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- "respondent": a person against whom a claim is made, or who is joined as a respondent; for Part 2 also a person against whom a claimant intends to make a claim.
-- src:252 | “respondent” means a person against whom a claim is made, or
-- src:253 | who is joined in the capacity of a respondent, and includes,
-- src:254 | for the purposes of Part 2, a person against whom a claimant
-- src:255 | intends to make a claim;
@ref s 2(1) “respondent” (src:252-255)
GIVEN `a claim is made against the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is joined in the capacity of a respondent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a claimant intends to make a claim against the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the question is asked for the purposes of Part 2` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) the person is a respondent` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `a claim is made against the person` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the person is joined in the capacity of a respondent` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the question is asked for the purposes of Part 2` AND `a claimant intends to make a claim against the person` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“respondent” means a person against whom a claim is made, or who is joined in the capacity of a respondent"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

