`s 2(1) the dispute is a wrongful dismissal dispute` MEANS
    IF dispute's `relates to the dismissal of an employee`
    THEN CONSIDER dispute's matter
         WHEN `A matter in the Third Schedule` item THEN JUST TRUE
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“wrongful dismissal dispute” means a dispute, relating to the dismissal of an employee, specified in the Third Schedule"
         WHEN `A matter in the First Schedule` item THEN JUST FALSE
         WHEN `A matter in the Second Schedule` item THEN JUST FALSE
         WHEN `None of the matters in the Schedules` THEN JUST FALSE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“wrongful dismissal dispute” means a dispute, relating to the dismissal of an employee"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- "specified employment dispute": a specified contractual dispute, a specified statutory dispute or a wrongful dismissal dispute.
-- src:268 | “specified employment dispute” means a specified contractual
-- src:269 | dispute, a specified statutory dispute or a wrongful dismissal
-- src:270 | dispute;
@ref s 2(1) “specified employment dispute” (src:268-270)
GIVEN dispute IS A Dispute
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) the dispute is a specified employment dispute` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 2(1) the dispute is a specified contractual dispute` dispute EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `s 2(1) the dispute is a specified statutory dispute` dispute EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `s 2(1) the dispute is a wrongful dismissal dispute` dispute EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“specified employment dispute” means a specified contractual dispute, a specified statutory dispute or a wrongful dismissal dispute"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:276 | “tribunal” means a subordinate court called an Employment
-- src:277 | Claims Tribunal constituted under section 4 of the State
-- src:278 | Courts Act 1970;
@ref s 2(1) “tribunal” (src:276-278)
GIVEN `it is a subordinate court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is called an Employment Claims Tribunal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was constituted under section 4 of the State Courts Act 1970` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
